    "description": "Tree farm, level 2 of 3: L1 plus flourish 2. Over budget: 323 blocks vs 102 (the lumber camp brief; the tree farm has no budget of its own), first build 254 vs 200. The lumber camp's tier-6 upgrade: an 11 x 11 fenced plantation (spruce fence on capped cobblestone corner piers, a timber gateway) with rows of young trees either side of a coarse dirt path, the woodcutter's 5 x 4 gabled shed at the back in the sawmill's look (dark oak frame, spruce walls, oak roof with dark oak eaves; oak door; chest, grindstone workstation, barrel) and a log yard. L1: plot, shed, four rows of young trees (log stem and leaf head), log pile, chopping block, composter. L2: oak and birch sapling rows between them, a lychgate roof with lanterns, lanterns on the piers, window shutters, a sawhorse, cauldron and barrel. L3: a lean-to drying shed over the log yard, a hanging sign (the Studio does not draw hanging signs), banners by the shed door, a shelf of potted saplings, flowers, moss, an axe in the block. Not yet builder-tested: birch_sapling, cauldron, oak_sapling.",
    "changes": "Quality check round 1: young trees (log stem, leaf head) in the L1 rows instead of bare dirt; caps on the corner piers; the two big oaks that ran into the shed are gone; the shed is now a real 5 x 4 gabled shed with a door and windows; L3 adds a lean-to drying shed over the log yard.",
